>   - /usr/sbin/service nginx restart
> \`\`\`
>
> Not suggested: 1 with arguments that look like a secret, 1 run as another user.
>
> A sudo allowlist is not a boundary: a command that can run code or write files gives the job root, and root can remove the egress controls. Enforce with any \`sudo-config\` is ADVISORY. Best effort: the sudo log does not show \`sudo -E\` or where one argument ends and the next begins, so a command shown as allowed can still be refused in enforce.


**✅ Nothing would be blocked.** 4 hosts · 5 requests · 3.3 MiB through the proxy.

