| Host | Requests | Data | Responses |
|:--|--:|--:|:--|
| \`registry.npmjs.org\` <sub>🔀 passthrough</sub> | 2 | ↑ 600 B ↓ 3.0 MiB | 2xx (1)<br>4xx (1) |
| \`archive.ubuntu.com\` <sub>plain HTTP</sub> | 1 | ↑ 200 B ↓ 256.0 KiB | 2xx (1) |

<sub>🔀 passthrough = checked by TLS name only — not decrypted, so no byte counts.</sub>

<details>
<summary>🐙 <b>GitHub platform</b> — 3 hosts · 2 requests · 4.2 KiB · expected for every job</summary>

| Host | Requests | Data | Responses |
|:--|--:|--:|:--|
| \`api.github.com\` | 2 | ↑ 240 B ↓ 4.0 KiB | 2xx (1)<br>3xx (1) |
| \`hosted-compute-abc.githubapp.com\` <sub>🔀 passthrough</sub> | — | n/a | n/a |
| \`productionresultssa1.blob.core.windows.net\` | 0 | — | — |

<sub>🔀 passthrough = checked by TLS name only — not decrypted, so no byte counts.</sub>

</details>

<details open>
<summary>🐳 <b>Container egress</b> — 2 containers · ⚠️ 1 container did not trust the CA · 1 outside the proxy rejected</summary>

<sub>Traffic from Docker containers (service containers, \`docker run\`, \`docker build\`) goes through the same proxy and DNS filter. 🔀 = checked by TLS name only, no CA needed in the container.</sub>

| Container | Allowed | Blocked | Outside the proxy |
|:--|:--|:--|:--|
| \`redis\`<br><sub>172.17.0.2</sub> | 🔀 \`registry.npmjs.org\` | \`ctr-exfil.example.net\` | ❌ \`198.51.100.8:123\` UDP |
| \`172.17.0.3\` | \`productionresultssa1.blob.core.windows.net\` | — | — |

**TLS failed because the container did not trust the runtime CA:** \`172.17.0.3\` → \`productionresultssa1.blob.core.windows.net\`. Containers need no CA, except for multi-tenant front doors (Azure Storage): those stay intercepted so the Host check still stops fronting to another tenant. Reach them from a step on the runner, or give the container the CA (\`/etc/safer-runner/ca.pem\`).

</details>

<details>
<summary>🔧 <b>Diagnostics</b> — self-tests 3/3 ✓ · 2 non-proxy destinations rejected · no workflow sudo (1 by Safer Runner) · docker removed ✓ · config unchanged ✓</summary>

**Self-tests**

- ✅ \`sni-block\` — SNI selftest.safer-runner.invalid -\\> BLOCK (sni-not-allowed); curl exit 35
- ✅ \`repoint\` — client dialled 192.0.2.1, proxy connected to 140.82.112.3:443 (HTTP 200)
- ✅ \`dns-exact\` — srst-abc.objects.githubusercontent.com -\\> NXDOMAIN; DNS log labels it BLOCK

**Outside the proxy** <sub>(only TCP 80/443 is proxied; new connections only; logging rate-limited to 60/min)</sub>

| Destination | Proto | Likely | UID | Packets | Result |
|:--|:--|:--|--:|--:|:--|
| \`1.1.1.1:853\` | TCP | DNS-over-TLS | 1001 | 2 | ❌ rejected |
| \`198.51.100.7:22\` | TCP | SSH | 1001 | 1 | ❌ rejected |

**Sudo** — the workflow ran none; Safer Runner itself ran 1 (setup, integrity checks).

**Docker** — \`docker: remove-group\`; verified at setup: runner user removed from the docker group, socket root-only

**Config file tamper check** (advisory) — all verified

**Configuration Files**

| File | Status |
|--|--|
| /etc/resolv.conf | VERIFIED |


<sub>The tamper check and this summary come from the post step, which runs as the runner user from files the job's steps can modify: an advisory tripwire, not tamper-proof evidence. The egress controls themselves are root-owned and don't depend on it.</sub>

</details>

<sub>enforce · job \`build\` · 2026-11-07 12:34 UTC · [Safer Runner Action](https://github.com/portswigger-tim/safer-runner-action) v2</sub>
"
`;

